architecture client-organs
  canonical_name ClientOrgans
  family surface
  domain Surface / Browser capabilities the server cannot reach
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What can a browser add to a page this estate already composed, without becoming a second compositor or a second source of truth?
  purpose Four capabilities a server cannot provide from a distance -- showing what changed, anchoring an explanation beside the thing it explains, keeping an enormous list navigable, and spending the reader's own idle hardware instead of the estate's. Each is a vendored library bound to markup the estate already emits, so it reaches every surface at once rather than page by page.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ClientOrgan
  node_types VendoredLibrary
  node_types BoundaryAperture
  edge_types binds_to
  edge_types enhances
  internal_calculus an organ binds to selectors the estate already emits -- .region, ol.more, .src, .by, [data-bf-slot] -- so breadth comes from the estate's own vocabulary rather than from per-page wiring
  internal_calculus every organ is absent-tolerant: a vendored file that does not load leaves the page exactly as it arrived, because the page was already complete when it arrived
  internal_calculus a boundary aperture moves the estate's own sentence and never rewrites it; an aperture that paraphrased a boundary would be stating a weaker one
  internal_calculus a chart draws the points the server computed and interpolates nothing, because a line between two observations is a claim nobody made
  internal_calculus libraries are vendored and served by this estate rather than fetched from anyone's CDN at read time, so a reader's page does not depend on a third party being up or honest
  invariant the browser composes nothing: no organ decides what a page says, what material it carries, or what anyone may do
  invariant browser state covers only what this reader is looking at; it is never durable, never shared, and never a fact about the estate
  invariant a composed public page carries at most one script, and only where something plays; the organs ride a script such a page already has and never add one
  invariant an organ that cannot start records why in window.bfOrganErrors rather than failing silently
  forbidden_inference an organ running -> the browser holding authority, or the page having been composed here
  forbidden_inference a reordered or animated list -> a change in what the estate holds
  forbidden_inference an aperture opening -> any claim beyond the sentence the server already published
  source_path site/matrix/client-organs.js
  source_path site/matrix/world.css
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness 2026-09-25 measured in a real browser against the live estate: on aurekai.work/economics seven organs bound with zero failures -- 12 containers animated, 28 boundary notes scanned and 19 made openable, one chart drawn from 7 days of real meter data -- and on nick.aurekai.life 60 containers across 33 slots
  witness 2026-09-25 an aperture opened on click, anchored by Floating UI, carrying the estate's own accrual sentence verbatim: "Accrued use is what this estate's reading would cost at rates it has admitted with evidence"
  witness 2026-09-25 window.bfAsk reached the live machine aperture from the page, searched the estate for "permit" and got two retained things back, and the same path refused media_transport_lease with the reason that a lease is an effect the edge holds no authority to grant
  known_gap two organs remain wired and unexercised: tiles registers no basemap because no PMTiles archive is published yet, and space indexes nothing because no surface emits data-bf-points -- the field builds its own index rather than handing points to that organ. Each is a capability available to the next surface that needs it, not a capability in use
  witness 2026-09-25 the offload organ stopped being a capability and became a caller: the field hands it /assets/field-index.worker.js and gets back a finished Flatbush index over 109,761 points, built on another thread, and the page says so
  known_gap the first loader identified a UMD library by diffing window after the script ran. A global declared with var is not enumerable, so every UMD organ silently received an empty object while the libraries loaded perfectly; the exports are now named. The silent catch that hid this is why organ failures are now recorded where a reader can see them
  known_gap the aperture dismissal was first registered once per note, so opening one aperture fired eighteen listeners that each shut it again; it is registered once
  internal_calculus a composed public page fetches no renderer at all, so it gets the one enhancement obtainable without a library: the aperture, written inline into the single script such a page already carries. Motion, charts, spatial indexes and worker offload stay on the surfaces where fetching a library is allowed
  witness 2026-09-25 aurekai.live composed: one inline script, nothing fetched, and its boundary note opens as an anchored aperture carrying the server's own sentence -- page_composition's "no renderer is fetched or mounted" and "at most one script" both still pass
  known_gap the inline aperture positions itself arithmetically rather than through a collision-aware engine, because loading one would be the fetch this page forbids; near a viewport edge it is clamped rather than flipped
  known_gap four of the surveyed libraries were not vendored: Orama shipped only a bare re-export, regl-scatterplot needs a peer that is not here, and VanJS and Mediabunny answered 404 at the versions tried
  internal_calculus the list organ positions rows the server already sent and renders none of them. A virtualizer that insisted on rendering would have to become the renderer, and then the room would exist twice; measuring and placing is the only part a browser does better than the server
  internal_calculus the list organ refuses below sixty rows, because under that there is nothing to win and the cost is a scroll container where the page had none
  internal_calculus a virtualised list states its own length on the page, since a list that scrolls without saying how long it is hides its own size
  invariant a reader with scripting off receives every row of a virtualised list as ordinary HTML, because the rows were in the document before the organ touched them
  forbidden_inference a virtualised list -> rows fetched on demand; nothing is requested as a reader scrolls, and the count on the page is the count that was sent
  witness 2026-09-26 the promise in this entry's own purpose -- keeping an enormous list navigable -- had no organ behind it until now. @tanstack/virtual-core 3.13.12 is vendored at 14,349 bytes with its digest and licence recorded, and the list organ binds every [data-bf-list] the estate emits
  witness 2026-09-26 measured against the organ's exact option set: 502 rows at 34px give a 17,068px scroll and 20 rows to lay out -- twelve in view and eight of overscan -- so erpnext's 502 record kinds cost the browser twenty rows instead of five hundred
  witness 2026-09-26 /s/apps/crm and /s/apps/erpnext serve one data-bf-list each with 44 and 502 server-rendered rows, and /assets/vendor-vlist.min.js answers 200 with the recorded bytes
  interacts client-organs-enhance-composed-pages

interaction client-organs-enhance-composed-pages
  source client-organs
  destination web-address-edge
  relation enhances_without_composing
  preserves the server as the only compositor and the only source of what a page says
  drops any path by which a browser could decide material, authority, or what a boundary means
  forbidden_inference a page carrying organs -> a page whose content the browser had any part in choosing
  witness 2026-09-25 the estate's own page_composition test refused a second script tag on a composed page and the tag was withdrawn rather than the invariant relaxed; the enhancement was rewritten to fit inside the one inline script those pages already carry
  binding site/matrix/client-organs.js
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c

architecture estate-field
  canonical_name EstateField
  family surface
  domain Surface / The whole estate at once
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What does a hundred and nine thousand addresses actually look like, and how many of them does this estate really read?
  purpose Every channel address the ledger holds, drawn as one field in the reader's own graphics hardware, from the estate's own columnar catalogue read out of the object store by byte range. Its axes are the ledger's columns, so the shape of the picture is the shape of the data.
  maturity implemented
  node_types FieldPoint
  node_types CatalogueRead
  edge_types drawn_from
  internal_calculus across is truth_level -- how this estate came to know of the address at all; up is state -- how far that address got; colour is protocol. Scatter inside a cell is deterministic from the channel id so a point keeps its place between visits, and carries no meaning
  internal_calculus a row or column nothing landed in is not drawn, because an empty band is a shape a reader will try to read
  internal_calculus an admitted channel is drawn at full weight and a candidate as a haze, which is the actual difference between a source and a record of an address
  internal_calculus the query engine runs in the reader's tab against Parquet in the object store; no server composes the field, and the estate pays for no query
  internal_calculus a channel is named by the root that publishes it, joined from source_root in the same catalogue, because a reader knows "BBC Sport" and nobody knows a feedburner URL
  internal_calculus a click asks two different things the same question and shows both answers: the catalogue already open in this tab, by SQL over bytes read from the object store, and the estate's own read-only aperture over the wire. Neither is a reading of the source, and the page says which answer came from where
  internal_calculus the channel is registered under the host that serves it and what was kept is filed under the publisher it came from -- feeds.bbci.co.uk against bbci.co.uk. The join matches on the tail rather than pretending the whole host matched
  internal_calculus the spatial index over a hundred thousand points is built on another thread when the offload organ is present, because the first seconds of the field are the ones a reader judges it by
  invariant the browser draws the catalogue and never edits it; a point is a published row and nothing here writes one
  forbidden_inference a point in the field -> a source this estate reads; the overwhelming majority are candidates nothing has admitted
  forbidden_inference an address appearing here -> that it answers, that it carries what it claims, or that this estate endorses it
  source_path site/matrix/field.html
  witness 2026-09-25 live at aurekai.work/field: DuckDB-Wasm read 109,761 rows from source_channel.parquet in R2 by byte range inside the tab, and WebGPU drew them on the device's own hardware -- 2,364 of them admitted, which is the whole point of drawing the rest
  witness 2026-09-25 measured live on aurekai.live/field: the join to source_root matched all 109,761 channels with none unmatched, and a hovered point named BBC Sport - Tennis rather than its feed URL
  witness 2026-09-25 a click on that point returned both answers -- six things kept from bbci.co.uk read in the tab out of material.parquet, and five more from the aperture over the wire for the same publisher -- with the panel naming which came from where
  interacts estate-field-asks-the-aperture
  interacts field-reads-the-catalogue
  known_gap kin and neighbour hold 710 and 317 rows from one source, so drawing them would be a picture of that source rather than of the estate; material is now read, but only on a click and only by publisher
  known_gap there is no WebGPU fallback path beyond a single static canvas draw, and it says so rather than pretending to be the same surface
  source_path site/matrix/field-keeper.js
  source_path deploy/worker/estate-worker.mjs
  internal_calculus the catalogue is kept in the device's private file store beside the stamp the estate gave it. Each visit asks with that stamp: unchanged sends nothing, changed replaces the kept copy, and an estate out of reach is answered from the kept copy with the page saying so. A device with no private file store keeps nothing and reads by byte range as before
  internal_calculus the page, the query engine and its scripts are kept by a worker registered for /field alone. The engine and its worker script are fetched by the page and handed over as bytes, because a worker's own requests are not asked of that keeper; the off-thread index worker loads its own scripts, so with the estate out of reach the index is built in the page
  invariant a kept copy without its stamp is never read; the stamp is written after the bytes
  invariant the page states which copy it read: first kept, unchanged, replaced, or the kept copy with the estate out of reach
  witness 2026-10-03 in Chrome against a local stand-in for the edge serving this page, its assets and the real 11 MB catalogue: first visit kept three files (2.9, 1.0 and 7.5 MB) and drew 109,762 records; a reload answered all three with 304 and downloaded nothing; after one file was republished with 50,000 rows the reload fetched that file alone and drew 50,000; with the server stopped the page opened, read the kept copy, drew on WebGPU and said the estate could not be reached
  source_path site/matrix/tests/field-kept-copy.test.mjs
  witness site/matrix/tests/field-kept-copy.test.mjs runs the page in a real browser across five separate browser processes on one profile, against a local stand-in for the edge cut from the estate's own catalogue: first visit keeps three files and draws 4,000 records; a fresh process downloads nothing (three 304s); after one file is republished that file alone is fetched and 1,500 records are drawn; with the server stopped the page opens, reads the kept copy, draws and says the estate could not be reached; when it returns the copy is confirmed current
  forbidden_inference the 2026-10-03 witness -> the published field behaving so; the page, the keeper and the edge's 304 answer are in source and none has been published
  forbidden_inference a field drawn with the estate out of reach -> a current catalogue; it is the copy from the last visit and says so
  known_gap the kept-copy path is witnessed on a local stand-in for the edge, not on the published estate: field-keeper.js is not yet published at the site root and the edge worker's conditional answer is not deployed. Until it is, a visit re-downloads the catalogue and the page reports it unchanged by comparing stamps
  known_gap a device's private file store belongs to one origin, so the kept catalogue is held once for each Aurekai domain a reader visits: all four is four copies of the same 11 MB. Nothing shares one copy between them
  known_gap a first visit now downloads the two tables it draws whole (about 4 MB) rather than reading them by byte range, and keeps the third (7.5 MB) in the background
  known_gap with the estate out of reach a click is answered from the kept catalogue only; the aperture's answer over the wire is absent. The field writes nothing, so there is nothing of the reader's to reconcile, and no collaborative or draft state is kept here
  known_gap the catalogue is a publication, so the field is as current as the last publish pass rather than live

interaction estate-field-asks-the-aperture
  source estate-field
  destination web-address-edge
  relation reads_through
  preserves the aperture's read-only aperture: the field calls tools that return what the estate kept and nothing that performs an effect
  drops any path by which drawing the catalogue could write to it, or by which a click could reach the source itself
  forbidden_inference an answer in the field -> a fresh reading of that source; both answers are things this estate already retained
  forbidden_inference a point that answers -> an address that still publishes what was kept from it
  witness 2026-09-25 clicking a point on the live field reached /mcp with estate_search and rendered five retained things; the same page's other question was answered locally by DuckDB-Wasm, and the two agreed
  binding site/matrix/field.html
  binding deploy/worker/estate-worker.mjs

architecture service-site
  canonical_name ServiceSite
  family surface
  domain Surface / A service business's public site, built from one record
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What pages and sections does a service business's site have, in whose words, where do a visitor's requests go, and how does a second business get one without a second builder?
  purpose A kit of fifteen sections (hero, ask, door, proof, steps, compare, cases, person, reviews, listings, figures, calculator, amounts, library, call) around a shared shell. A page's one request form sits in its hero or in an ask section. A library section publishes a large collection as small compressed pieces (entries in runs, each kind's titles in pages, title words by first letters) that a phone fetches only on request, and says how much it has fetched. A site shows the contact routes it has; phone, name and email are each optional when the site keeps requests itself. A site is one record: the business, the contact, pages of ordered sections with their words, and a look. The look is stated in the same roles a presentation template carries, so a site can wear an authored estate language by name or state its own; every shade is worked out from those roles and an unreadable look is refused at build. The form is flat or stepped, with typed fields and stated choices. A site either hands requests to the visitor's mail app or keeps them with its own small server code, which accepts only the fields its own forms ask for; kept requests are brought into the CMS as service_lead rows. The record lives in the CMS as a service_site entry, is exported to the site folder, built to static pages with a stylesheet holding only what they use, and published to the Cloudflare account the record names.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SiteRecord, SitePage, SiteSection, SiteLook, SiteRequest
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/build.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/theme.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/looks/editorial.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/looks/night.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/shell.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/form.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/lead-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/library.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/ask.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/door.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/amounts.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/library.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/cloud.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/site.mjs
  source_path deploy/launchd/com.bonfyre.service-site-leads.plist
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/hero.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/proof.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/steps.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/compare.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/cases.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/person.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/reviews.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/listings.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/figures.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/calculator.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/call.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/fixtures/sample-lawn/content.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/service_site.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/service_lead.json
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs builds two businesses from two records, serves each as it is published (files plus the site's own server code) and uses them in Chrome at 320, 390, 768, 1024 and 1280 wide: no failed load, script error or third-party script; on a phone nothing runs off the screen, every control is at least 44 px tall, no text is under 12 px, no field makes the phone zoom, and the menu opens and closes; a stepped form refuses to advance unfilled, the request it sends is kept with only what was typed, and when the server cannot keep it the mail app gets it and the page says so; the server code refuses another origin, another form, an unlisted field, an unstated choice, a missing phone, an oversized body, and keeps nothing from a filled trap field
  witness 2026-10-04 on the live site six requests from one address were answered 201 five times and then 429, and the browser fell back to the mail app; after the counter was cleared a marked request sent through the live buyers form on a phone was picked up by the scheduled job, became a service_lead row and a held outbound_message addressed to the business, and was then removed from the site and the CMS
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs also searches, browses and reads a 1,000-entry collection on a phone-sized browser: nothing of it is fetched before a search, a 700-entry kind arrives a page at a time, an entry opens and deep-links, a title containing markup stays text, the whole visit takes under fourteen small pieces, and with no contact on record a request the server cannot keep is said to have failed
  witness 2026-10-05 the editorial look, drawn in Google Stitch from a brief written off the estate's own surfaces and applied by hand from its design system and screens (the editor took no automated pointer input, so its code was not exported), is live on https://aurekai-recipes.pages.dev/: serif roman and italic headline, paper and ink bands, numbered facts, hairline tables; no sideways scroll and no small tap target at 320 and 390 wide
  witness 2026-10-04 published from the live CMS record to a second Cloudflare account; every live page opened in Chrome at phone and desk width, one marked test request sent through the live form answered 201, was brought into the CMS by site.mjs leads exactly once across two runs, and was then removed from both
  invariant a section never names a colour and the shell never names a business; what differs between two sites is in their records
  invariant a look is a named way of drawing the same sections (the kit has two: editorial and night); it changes no word, no order and no behaviour, and a record cannot name a look the kit does not have
  invariant a review, a listing or a table of figures appears only when it is on file whole (a review with who said it, a listing with place and price, figures with source and day read); otherwise the section, its menu link, and a page left with nothing but its opening are absent
  invariant a record can ask for material only by a name the site folder provides; a record never runs anything
  invariant a library page holds none of its collection and fetches nothing of it until asked; titles and entries are placed as text, never as markup
  invariant an amounts section only switches between lists worked before the page was built; nothing is calculated in the browser
  invariant a request's own records can be consulted as it arrives through the site folder's lead hook, which reads and contacts nobody
  invariant the server code keeps a request only from this site's own origin, for a form this site has, with only that form's fields and stated choices, and records nothing about the visitor beyond what they typed
  invariant the page says a request was kept only after the server answered that it was; otherwise it says the mail app has it
  invariant a sender is counted under a one-way mark of its network address that lives an hour and is never stored with a request
  invariant bringing a request into the CMS writes a held message for the business and sends nothing
  invariant while the record says preview, the pages and the edge both tell search engines not to index it, and the page lists what the owner has yet to confirm
  forbidden_inference a section filled in -> the statement in it is true or confirmed by the business; the kit checks shape and readability, never facts
  forbidden_inference a request kept -> the business has seen it, a verified person sent it, or anybody agreed to anything beyond being answered
  forbidden_inference a site wearing an estate template -> the site is part of the estate, served by it, or governed by its address
  forbidden_inference a record in the CMS -> an engagement with that business or authority to publish for it
  forbidden_inference a site on a named Cloudflare account -> that account belongs to the business
  known_gap the business is not told by this estate when a request arrives: every ten minutes a job on this Mac brings requests into the CMS, tells whoever is at the Mac, and holds a message addressed to the business for a person to send. If this Mac is off, requests wait at the site (up to 180 days)
  known_gap the limits (five an hour from one network address, three hundred a day for a site) are counted in a store that is not instantly consistent, so a burst can pass slightly over
  known_gap a service site is published to Cloudflare Pages on purpose and is not a site_program: the web-address organ does not serve it, and estate material reaches it only as build-time material the site folder provides
  known_gap only the six authored templates can be worn by name; the compiled Ghost reference census is not read
  known_gap the editorial look restyles the existing markup through its section kinds; it is not a second set of layouts. Fleming's site wears the night look instead; neither look has photographs of its own, and the night look's one backdrop is a low-resolution crop of a supplied design
  known_gap the checks written against Fleming's record of 2026-10-04 are skipped unless that earlier record is supplied; the current record is checked by completion.test.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/fleming-revision.test.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/fleming-revision.test.mjs applies owner-provided content, colours and section ordering through existing renderSite and the original generated worker, without creating another site builder
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/navigation.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/seo.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/prose.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/completion.test.mjs
  invariant optional authored navigation and calls to action address existing local pages or anchors; a dead local route fails the build
  invariant select and multiline inquiry fields lower through the existing form and lead consumer rather than a second application
  invariant canonical and social metadata and sitemap are projected from the same site record; preview indexing remains disabled and no ratings or licensing status is inferred
  invariant lead body intake counts at most 8000 UTF-8 bytes before parsing; blank required values, mismatched origins, undeclared fields and excessive field sizes are refused
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/completion.test.mjs passes 8 tests and 45 assertions for local links, metadata, input types, body bounds, exact origin, blank refusal and preserved rate limits
  witness 2026-10-05 the unchanged fourteen-test ServiceSite regression passed 270 assertions using its earlier private Fleming fixture and the existing sample site
  forbidden_inference the authored terms and privacy preview pages -> legal approval or a complete public-launch privacy policy

  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/catalogue.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/catalogue-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/catalogue-model.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/catalogue-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/catalogue.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/catalogue-model.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/catalogue-browser.test.mjs
  invariant a catalogue workspace is a dedicated page without a marketing hero; it uses the site's checked colour and font roles
  invariant catalogue edits retain source product and option identifiers and the source snapshot digest; a draft never changes the retained catalogue
  invariant published catalogue pieces are checksummed before use; their local store module is copied from the existing browser workbench at build time, never maintained separately
  invariant a saved catalogue draft is a browser-local revision checked atomically against its previous revision, so a stale tab cannot overwrite a newer draft
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/catalogue-model.test.mjs checks decimal cents, invalid values, source identity, draft restoration and checksummed packaging
  witness 2026-10-07 components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/catalogue-browser.test.mjs passes 26 checks in fresh Chrome processes over the retained Redwood Rings and AJ Collectives catalogues: edit and review, reload and browser restart, stale-tab conflict, service items, store switching, empty and failed loads, corrupted piece, and 320/390/768/1440 layouts
  forbidden_inference a saved catalogue draft -> a change published to Shopify, an authorized merchant session, or a draft synchronized between devices
  known_gap catalogue drafts currently remain in this browser; merchant-account publication and shared draft submission are not connected to this workspace

interaction catalogue-reuses-browser-drafts
  source service-site
  destination browser-host
  relation uses_browser_local_draft_store
  preserves source identity, prior revision and saved edits
  drops extension capture and native-host operations, which this page does not invoke
  forbidden_inference a shared store module -> a shared database across web origins
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/catalogue-browser.test.mjs
  binding integrations/browser/extension/store.mjs

architecture fleming-site
  canonical_name FlemingSite
  family surface
  domain Surface / A prospect's public site, built from a record
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What does Fleming Equity Group's site say, who decided each statement, and how does a change reach the live link?
  purpose Fleming Equity Group's site: one service-site record and two pictures. Two pages: selling a house in Dallas (a three-step request form) and a buyers page (a list to join, a sum to work, and properties only when some are on file). It speaks of Dallas County only, as the user stated on 2026-10-04. The design came from generated mock-ups; every fact comes from the record, and the mock-ups' invented deals, totals, people and numbers are not carried. The record is kept in the internal CMS and published to a Cloudflare account separate from the estate's.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SiteContent
  source_path packs/fleming-equity-group/site/content.json
  source_path packs/fleming-equity-group/site/lead.mjs
  source_path packs/fleming-equity-group/site/lead.test.mjs
  source_path packs/fleming-equity-group/actors.yaff
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/site.mjs
  witness packs/fleming-equity-group/site/lead.test.mjs resolves a typed address to its account on the Dallas County roll the pack holds, with owner of record, class, legal description and the pack's programme readiness, and says so when an address is not on the roll or cannot be read
  witness 2026-10-04 a marked seller request sent to the live site was picked up by the scheduled job, matched to one account on the roll, and its brief written into the request record and the held message; then removed
  witness 2026-10-04 published from the live CMS record to the second Cloudflare account: https://fleming-equity-group-16q.pages.dev/ and its buyers page open in Chrome at 320, 390 and 1280 wide with no failed load, script error or sideways scroll and no mention of Tarrant, Fort Worth or DFW; the removed market page answers 404, and the edge answers X-Robots-Tag noindex
  witness 2026-10-04 Google Maps' public listing for Fleming Equity Group LLC shows the same name and phone as the site (recorded in packs/fleming-equity-group/actors.yaff)
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs checks, where the private pack is present, that every word on the home page is in the record or is the kit's own label and that no place outside Dallas is named
  internal_calculus the generated mock-ups named a managing partner, a second principal, a phone number, an email domain, an office address, client reviews, closed volume, unallocated capital, title partners, accreditations, six properties with prices and spreads, a live assignment feed and a table of market yields, none of which are in anything this estate holds about Fleming. The name, phone and email were replaced with those observed on the Fleming flyer; the rest were removed, and the pages they sat on were rebuilt around what can be shown honestly
  internal_calculus the mock-up's form discarded what was typed and told the visitor it had been logged, and its stepped form ended in an invented price range. The stepped form is kept without the range, and what is typed is kept by the site or handed to the mail app
