architecture recipe-library-site
  canonical_name RecipeLibrarySite
  family surface
  domain Surface / A recipe catalogue of bases and their variations
  layer presentation
  semantic_question Which dishes in the collection are one base told many ways, and how does somebody find and read one on a phone?
  purpose The recipe site's own catalogue, on the site and in its look. Its entries come from the recipe organ's family transformation: recipes for the same dish that list the same ingredients in the same amounts are one entry showing the base once and each variation as what it adds, with that variation's own method; a recipe told several times unchanged is shown once; every other recipe stands alone. It is searched, browsed by kind and read through the kit's library section.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SiteContent, RecipeFamily
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sites/recipe-library/content.json
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sites/recipe-library/material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/library.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/library.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreRecipe/tools/derive_families.mjs
  witness 2026-10-05 the transformation run over the 159,328 gathered recipes gave 99,687 catalogue entries: 16,934 families holding 35,687 distinct variations, 17,979 recipes that were one recipe retold, 40,888 retellings folded
  witness 2026-10-05 on https://aurekai-recipes.pages.dev/ a phone-sized Chrome browsed the families, searched, and opened a family showing its base and its ways; the page has no link out to another site for its catalogue and no script error
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs opens a family in the library and checks the base is shown once, each way lists what it adds, the first way is open, and a way's name containing markup stays text
  invariant an ingredient is in a family's base only when every member lists it with the same amount and unit; nothing is averaged, converted or assumed
  invariant a family says it was grouped by a rule and never cooked as a set, and each variation keeps its source's own method
  invariant the page shows recipes, not measurements of itself
  forbidden_inference a family -> a tested base, or that its variations are interchangeable in cooking
  forbidden_inference a recipe shown -> tested, safe, or suitable for any diet
  forbidden_inference published here -> the source's contributors or the catalogue's owner agreed to republication
  known_gap many two-way families differ only in how the source typed an ingredient, and a family is named from the last words of its members' titles, which is sometimes odd ("Bread Pan")
  known_gap the families are kept beside the organ's pack as a compressed record file and are not yet the pack's own records, so the organ's rooms on aurekai.life still list recipes flat
  known_gap republication terms for the full recipe text are not settled; the site is a preview and is not indexed
